From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Almeida Barrios <gabarrios2006@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:14:26 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] engine: an invite to a call is sent only once the server
 acked it with the person on the roster

AddParticipant and RingParticipant returned as soon as the stanza left the socket. An invite the server dropped (every one after the first, before the previous commit) was therefore reported as sent, and the caller was told the person had been invited while nobody rang (user logs, 2026-11-16).

The invite is now a request: sendParticipantInvite waits up to 15 s for the ack with the same id and succeeds only when it carries a roster that lists the invited person, which is what WhatsApp's server answered WhatsApp Web's invite with on 2026-11-17 (the user in state "outgoing", 0.3 s later). No ack, an error ack, an ack without a roster or a roster without the person are failures; none of them ends the call.

whatsmeow hands an ack with a waiter to the waiter and not to the node handlers, so this ack no longer reaches onCallAck: its roster is applied here, with the same log line.

Validated: engine_group_invite_ack_test.go (four tests), go test . ./signaling green. Not yet validated on a live call.
